<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh tea prices fall on poor foreign demand.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh tea prices fall on poor foreign demand.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladeshi tea prices dropped on a lack of overseas demand at the weekly auction, brokers said.</p>
<p>Buyers for Pakistan, Poland and Afghanistan were subdued.</p>
<p>The average price was 71.72 taka per kg, down 1.24 taka from previous sale.</p>
<p>Some 914,400 kg of teas were sold at the auction. The next sale will</p>
<p>be on August 26 with an offer of 1,185,000 kg.</p>
<p>($1 = 44.55 taka)</p>
</text>
